session Continuous_Path_Spaces = Levy_Prokhorov_Metric +
  description "
    Weak convergence of processes done properly: C([0,T],'b) as a Polish
    space with portmanteau, the continuous mapping theorem and
    Arzela-Ascoli; tightness of a family of path laws from increment moments
    alone, hence a weakly convergent subsequence of the path laws of any
    sequence of continuous L2 martingales from a common start whose
    compensators grow at a common bounded rate; quadratic variation as an adapted, everywhere-continuous
    path functional with a summable L2 rate, equal to the compensator of a
    continuous L2 martingale whose compensator grows at a bounded rate, with
    no boundedness hypothesis on the martingale -- and the exit
    time of a closed set by a continuous path, upper semicontinuous along
    weak convergence of path laws, with Berge's theorem for the supremum of
    its essential infimum over a weakly compact family of laws.
  "
  options [document = pdf, document_output = "output"]
  sessions
    Continuous_Time_Martingales
    Kolmogorov_Chentsov
    Semicontinuous_Analysis
  theories
    Difference_Quotients
    Increment_Tails
    Dyadic_Chaining
    Modulus_Tails
    Holder_Interpolation
    Equicontinuity
    Path_Space
    Path_Exit_Times
    Path_Tightness
    Path_Space_Infinite
    Pathwise_Quadratic_Variation
    Adapted_Quadratic_Variation
  document_files
    "root.tex"
    "root.bib"
